main/boost: don't package the stacktrace addr2line lib on 32-bit arm.

On armv7 (arm_32 b2 variants), Boost.Stacktrace's build config disables
the addr2line backend, so libboost_stacktrace_addr2line*.so is never
produced and the boost-stacktrace_addr2line-libs subpackage fails with
take(): 'usr/lib/libboost_stacktrace_addr2line*.so.*' did not match
anything. (The b2 configure summary also prints "boost.stacktrace.basic
: no" for some variants, but libboost_stacktrace_basic.so.1.91.0 is in
fact built — only addr2line is missing from destdir.) Chimera has no
32-bit arm binary repo, so this only shows up when self-building the
armv7 repo (observed on the Astro armv7 port, boost 1.91.0, clang 22.1.7
cross from x86_64).

Drop addr2line from _libs on armv7/armhf so neither the subpackage nor
its provides are emitted there.

--- a/main/boost/template.py
+++ b/main/boost/template.py
@@ -60,6 +60,11 @@
     "wserialization",
 ]

+# b2's config checks disable this stacktrace backend on 32-bit arm
+# (arm_32: "boost.stacktrace.addr2line : no"); the lib is never built
+if self.profile().arch in ("armv7", "armhf"):
+    _libs.remove("stacktrace_addr2line")
+
 match self.profile().arch:
     case "ppc64le" | "ppc64" | "ppc":
         _arch, _abi = "power", "sysv"
